      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but it feels a bit vague. Could you go deeper into the legal/philosophical side of the \"causality\" argument? Like, what are the specific legal or moral principles opponents use to argue that current people shouldn't be liable for something that happened so long ago?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
