      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so basically the legal stuff is more about the difficulty of making it work rather than the actual morality of it? i've seen some people say that the argument about \"not being responsible for ancestors\" is just a way to dodge the actual harm that still exists today. do you think those arguments about personal responsibility are actually strong, or are they just used as an excuse to avoid addressing systemic issues?",
